<a id="intent-2-stop-flattening-associationupdate-properties-for"></a>
### 2. Stop flattening AssociationUpdate.properties for JavaScript.

| Change | Aspect | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ✏️ Modified | JavaScript client shape | AssociationUpdate properties are flattened. | AssociationUpdate properties remain nested. |

**TypeSpec change:** Scope the legacy flattenProperty customization away from JavaScript.

```diff
--- a/specification/servicenetworking/resource-manager/Microsoft.ServiceNetworking/ServiceNetworking/main.tsp
+++ b/specification/servicenetworking/resource-manager/Microsoft.ServiceNetworking/ServiceNetworking/main.tsp
@@ -82,7 +122,7 @@ model AssociationUpdate {

   /** The resource-specific properties for this resource. */
   #suppress "@azure-tools/typespec-azure-core/no-legacy-usage"
-  @Azure.ClientGenerator.Core.Legacy.flattenProperty
+  @Azure.ClientGenerator.Core.Legacy.flattenProperty("!javascript")
   properties?: AssociationUpdateProperties;
 }

```

**Impact:** [JavaScript property access changes from flattened to nested](#finding-pr-44200-js-nesting), [The stable version retains the replaced preview version](#finding-compliance-44200-stable-after-preview), [Private endpoint connections bypass the standard templates](#finding-compliance-44200-private-endpoint), [Private-link discovery bypasses the standard templates](#finding-compliance-44200-private-link), [Legacy flattening is applied to newly introduced models](#finding-compliance-44200-flattening)<br>
