<a id="finding-compliance-44200-flattening"></a>
### Legacy flattening is applied to newly introduced models

**Severity:** low

**Gap:** New private endpoint and private link resource properties use a legacy decorator that the reference does not recommend for greenfield types.

<details>
<summary><strong>Expected</strong></summary>

Do not add legacy flattening to newly introduced API models without an existing compatibility requirement.

**Guidance:** [TypeSpec Client Generator Core decorators — @Azure.ClientGenerator.Core.Legacy.flattenProperty](https://azure.github.io/typespec-azure/docs/libraries/typespec-client-generator-core/reference/decorators/)

_The guidance discourages the legacy decorator for new models; it does not prescribe replacement TypeSpec._

</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>Actual</strong></summary>

The new private endpoint and private link resource properties are flattened for AutoRest and C#.

**[back-compatible.tsp:L29-L38](https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/b1582b12f39f1d122fce3c7bbb24b812b0c5c487/specification/servicenetworking/resource-manager/Microsoft.ServiceNetworking/ServiceNetworking/back-compatible.tsp#L29-L38)**

```tsp
